    {
      "id": "1615468540368028",
      "createdAt": 1789778165,
      "text": "⚠️ Rolleston Prison PCO (Principal Corrections Officer) screwing Prisoners -\nKelly McDonald - Former PCO\n\nWe've been contacted by the mother of a former prisoner's son about some pretty disgusting conduct allegedly involving a Corrections officer at Rolleston Prison in Christchurch.\n\nShe says she discovered everything completely by accident. While going through the former prisoner's belongings, a shoebox fell and she discovered a collection of letters allegedly written to him by the Corrections officer. (Photos of the letters attached.)\n\nOne of those letters even states that the “PCO was up her ass this week” — referring to a Principal Corrections Officer — further tying the correspondence directly to her work inside the prison.\n\nShe says the officer would personally check and read his emails before handing them over to him, and even began using the same personal nicknames for him that were being used at home.\n\nShe says the officer pursued him during a roughly three-week period when his family wasn't visiting.\n\nWhat makes this particularly vile is that this same officer interacted with his family during visits. She would approach their table near the end, tap her nails and tell them they had around 10 minutes left. She even allegedly told his son, “Make sure you tell ‘Daddy’ you love him.” 🤢\n\nAccording to the information we've been given, it didn't stop at the prison gates. The officer allegedly visited him at his accommodation, arranged for her eldest child to babysit her children while she went to see him, and on the day of his release told him she had taken the day off and wanted to “tuck him in.” She then allegedly came to his house and picked him up.\n\nThere are also serious allegations that while he was still in custody, she brought cigarettes and other prohibited items into the prison for him.\n\nAfter the letters were discovered, the prison was contacted and a complaint was made. We're told the officer resigned on 11 September after the matter came to the prison's attention.\n\nThis isn't just about an affair. This man had a home and family waiting for him when he was released. After everything that has happened, that home is no longer waiting for him.\n\nThis is about a Corrections employee allegedly crossing serious professional boundaries with a prisoner she had access to through her job. If substantiated, the conduct described is disgusting, vile and completely unacceptable.\n\nToo much of what happens behind Corrections doors never reaches the public. They don't want their dirty laundry aired. We're using our platform to make sure this family's account isn't simply silenced or swept under the rug.\n\nThe evidence is attached. Corrections you're an absolute joke and this literally just proves it. Being able to get away with all that right under your nose. No wonder why so many unexplained deaths 👀\n\n#TrassssshyyyyBehaviour #Ew #Desperate",
      "url": "https://www.facebook.com/CheckpointNZ/posts/1615468540368028",
      "image": null
    },
